---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SheetEmbed from '../components/SheetEmbed.astro';

const bomSrc =
  "https://1drv.ms/x/c/1ab10ce1b91949c7/IQQmt6OwQfT6QpA4oYtTkpdgAfTlPQh_9JBAHBvyhKrCA38?em=2&AllowTyping=True&ActiveCell='BOM%2C%20base'!B2&wdHideGridlines=True&wdHideHeaders=True&wdDownloadButton=True&wdInConfigurator=True&wdInConfigurator=True&edaebf=rslc0";
---

<Base
  title="Denise Lin: Defense Program Cost Analysis"
  description="Denise Lin — defense program cost analysis: a bottoms-up Bill of Materials and Cost Element Structure built for a one-way attack drone program."
>
  <header class="hero wrap wrap--wide">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--gold">Defense Programs &middot; Cost Analysis</p>
    <h1 class="hero__name">Denise Lin</h1>
    <hr class="tick" />
  </header>

  <section class="wrap wrap--wide portfolio" aria-labelledby="port-h">
    <h2 id="port-h" class="portfolio__h">
      Drone Bill of Materials &amp; Cost Element Structure
    </h2>

    <div class="spotlight spotlight--hero">
      <div class="spotlight__copy">
        <p>
          I built a Bill of Materials and Cost Element Structure depicting
          procurement and operational costs for deployment of a Pygmy-Owl, a
          fictitious one-way attack drone meant to emulate the Shahed-136.
          This shows how I approach conceptualizing financial models and
          using data to inform program decisions.
        </p>
        <p>
          I used first principles to establish the format for the BOM (Tab 1
          in the spreadsheet), with the goal of conveying information in a
          way that is transparent/traceable and easy to read. I decided to
          break out the major Level 1 categories of Airframe, Launch System,
          and Ground Support Equipment so that the model has a clear sense of
          structure. I built a bottoms-up estimate using Level 3 items, so
          that the BOM estimate can be easily modified and improved if more
          accurate information becomes available for any given component.
        </p>
        <p>
          As someone with a background in running government programs, I
          know that reducing cost and increasing value is critical for
          securing government contracts. I identified potential cost
          improvements (Tab 3) by targeting the top six cost drivers. I
          researched feasible methods for cost reduction for these measures,
          reducing the total cost by 56%. I did a feasibility check of the
          estimate; I concluded the improved unit flyaway cost of $23,828 for
          materials is reasonable, because a comparable drone model, the
          LUCAS drone, is believed to cost $35,000 including both materials
          and labor.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lastly, I developed a Cost Element Structure to depict the
          operational cost of deploying Pygmy-Owls at scale. The purpose of
          this was to provide transparency into the full cost of running a
          mission, which goes well beyond munitions costs. I developed a CES
          as an example of a plan that could be used to justify program
          budgets and support a sustained mission deploying the Pygmy-Owl.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="spotlight__embed">
        <SheetEmbed
          hero={true}
          height={650}
          src={bomSrc}
          title="Pygmy-Owl Bill of Materials and Cost Element Structure, built by Denise Lin"
          caption="Live model: Pygmy-Owl Bill of Materials &amp; Cost Element Structure"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="contact">
        <a href="mailto:deniselihanlin@gmail.com">deniselihanlin@gmail.com</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="dot">&middot;</span>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/denise-lin"
          rel="me noopener"
          target="_blank">LinkedIn</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: clamp(3.5rem, 10vw, 6.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(0.25rem, 1.2vw, 0.6rem);
  }
  .hero__name {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }
  .hero__lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1rem + 0.35vw, 1.22rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 70ch;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .portfolio {
    padding-block: clamp(0.75rem, 2vw, 1.25rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
  }
  .portfolio__h {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .spotlight {
    padding: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
  }
  .spotlight--hero {
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--california-gold);
  }
  .spotlight__copy > :first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .spotlight__copy p {
    max-width: 82ch;
  }
  .spotlight__embed {
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
  }
</style>
